                <pb facs="0347" n="335" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg335"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">871.00/915: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gunther</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucharest</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-11-25T14:00:00+02:00">November 25,
                            1941—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 26—10:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>982. As it was in the beginning, feeling in the Rumanian Army is again becoming
                    increasingly bitter against the Germans and inasmuch as Marshal Antonescu
                    symbolizes the pro-German policy, he has lost much ground within army circles.
                    Countless minor incidents have been recounted to me which serve to show the way
                    the wind is blowing. For instance, the Rumanians had painfully combed out Odessa
                    for worthwhile war loot, such as tires and stores, and placed a guard over it
                    preparatory to removal to Rumania. The Germans brushed this guard aside and
                    grabbed the loot for themselves. The bare faced looting of Rumania proper by the
                    Germans of foodstuffs and other necessities has certainly not served to make
                    them better liked. This land of plenty for the first time since the war against
                    Germany is shadowed by the specter of want and in each case the reason is the
                    same, the Germans.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gunther</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
